#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:64
#: 6e814ad474a54731a8b51d8b69c0d187
msgid "OpenDroneID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:70
#: 58df7f07d8a54fbfb251811c12b98fb0
msgid "ArduPilot provides support for OpenDroneID in firmware versions 4.2 and later via MAVLink to an OpenDroneID compatible RemoteID module attached to either a serial port or DroneCAN port on the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:72
#: 9fd4e230eea44d8483983ce812f814bc
msgid "In order to provide tamper protection, a special autopilot firmware must be built and loaded on the autopilot which: enables this feature, prevents loading non-compliant firmware via GCS or normal uploaders, and provides further tamper-proofing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:74
#: f99a1a0f9dc14f6aa9f89d3dcf89b3e6
msgid "For details on building firmware with the OpenDroneID feature, see :ref:`dev:opendroneid` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:77
#: 645905e72a264e6ab2101c0a2e3e7326
msgid "ArduRemoteID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:79
#: b114d50b2e5d4836b740cb4f77438e07
msgid "ArduPilot also has developed firmware for  ESP32-S3 and C3 development boards for an OpenDroneID compatible Remote ID module for attachment by serial MAVLink connection or DroneCAN to the autopilot. A binary for flashing the board, along with instructions, is `available here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ArduRemoteID>`__.  Note, this firmware is rapidly evolving, so check for updates frequently. This device can be attached to the autopilot by USB, serial, or DroneCAN (if an external CAN transceiver is attached)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:84
#: 5afee0730b36410c8d4fa79afc3fb0cb
msgid "This firmware provides security signing and locking features for tamper resistance on the ArduRemoteID module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:86
#: aa445ac930ba4e7a970eb0d05f98e700
msgid "if the board has a USB programming port, access to that port, as well as the DroneCAN and MAVLink parameters, normally setup before shipment to customers can be locked, either temporarily or permanently, requiring a security key pair and secure commands to be used to alter those parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:87
#: 22d0933a403e4c0aaf2a03942e449437
msgid "when in a locked state, the only way to update firmware is to use a secure WIFI web interface provided by the module using a public/private key pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:89
#: aba60e6d248a4c2f82dad95d3fe357e0
msgid "See the detailed instructions in the `ArduRemoteID README.md file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ArduRemoteID>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:92
#: b3b8ae5a32f7417c861e95b25e1820c1
msgid "End User Data Setup and Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:94
#: a610058c68ff4bd3825273c3e652401a
msgid "Mission Planner (must be the latest beta version) has a tab in its DATA view (Drone ID) for OpenDrone ID operation which allows connection of the required external serial GPS to obtain operation location, and set up tabs for UAS and Operator IDs if required by your local jurisdiction. It also shows the Remote ID status. The ground station will also have status and pre-arm failure messages displayed if there are problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:97
